{:edb/db-before-t 1296 :edb/db-after-t 1297 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534609 50 #inst "2026-10-12T04:37:50.095Z" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067643 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067644 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067646 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186067647 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427576 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427578 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427580 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186067642 1075 #edb/ref 17592186427584 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186067642 1078 #edb/ref 17592186427584 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186068459 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\pi \\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186068459 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n![](images/d9/d9ed4c8dcfbbc0fe7b4bf58e58197598221fc730613005a719252bf88c07d3f4.svg)" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186068857 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427593 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186068859 1038 #edb/ref 17592186427592 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186068999 1050 420.0 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186069412 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186069412 1071 "Given that $r(t) = ⟨\\cos^{2} t, \\sin^{2} t⟩$, calculate $r(\\frac{π}{4})$." 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186069412 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨{cos}^{2}⁡t,\\,{sin}^{2}⁡t⟩,$ calculate $r(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186069412 1074 "We substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2},\\,{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186070011 1064 "We can also define vector-valued functions with three components. For example,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} (t) = t \\ \\mathbf{i} + 2t^2 \\ \\mathbf{j} + 3t^3 \\ \\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nThis particular definition uses the so-called $\\mathbf{i}$-$\\mathbf{j}$-$\\mathbf{k}$ notation.\n\nWe can represent the same function using **angle bracket** notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle t,  \\: 2t^2, \\: 3t^3 \\rangle\n$$\n\nAnother notation that's often convenient is **bracket** notation:\n\n![](images/a9/a95fd21b6ea5e7eae150b516d7d0ad82d283a31c895c9223abbeac81b622bb7d.svg)\n\nIt's important to realize that all three notations represent the same function." 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186070011 1064 "We can also define vector-valued functions with three components. For example,\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf f (t) = x(t) \\, \\mathbf{i} + y(t) \\, \\mathbf{j} + z(t) \\, \\mathbf{k}\n\\end{align*}\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} (t) = t \\ \\mathbf{i} + 2t^2 \\ \\mathbf{j} + 3t^3 \\ \\mathbf{k}.\n$$\n\nThis particular definition uses the so-called $\\mathbf{i}$-$\\mathbf{j}$-$\\mathbf{k}$ notation.\n\nWe can represent the same function using **angle bracket** notation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle t,  \\: 2t^2, \\: 3t^3 \\rangle\n$$\n\nAnother notation that's often convenient is **bracket** notation:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 2{t}^{2} \\\\ 3{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIt's important to realize that all three notations represent the same function." 13194139534609 17592186045417 false] [17592186427576 1080 "⟨2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427576 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427576 1083 #uuid "0f6a5f44-7c10-57f2-8e95-6bb68e1b82b1" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427577 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427577 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427577 1083 #uuid "2124c1b9-25d8-5849-a68d-2733cf6f9a90" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427578 1080 "⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,2⟩" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427578 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427578 1083 #uuid "2331cd21-2ed1-5625-a66c-71e5cb90700e" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427579 1080 "2" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427579 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427579 1083 #uuid "47a373d1-518e-59a4-aefc-060c414c4460" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427580 1080 "⟨2,\\,2⟩" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427580 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427580 1083 #uuid "4ac18ed6-58a3-5417-b730-cedc5302f322" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427581 1080 "⟨5,\\,8⟩" 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427581 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534609 17592186045417 true] [17592186427581 1083 #uuid "526cac9d-bee9-5e96-9ea8-424944084161" 13194139534609 17592186045417 tr